       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the maximum daily dose of ibuprofen. The usual maximum for adults is 3,200 mg/day, and the usual maximum single dose is 800 mg. At this dose the risks of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up sharply, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nHere are some common regimens. Which one did you mean?\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the maximum for inflammatory or pain indications.\n- **400\u2013600 mg PO every 6 hours** (1,600\u20132,400 mg/day), the usual dose for pain.\n- **1600 mg total per day**, divided into 400 mg four times daily. This may be where the number came from.\n\nIf you really do want 1600 mg four times daily, tell me the clinical reason and I'll enter it with a note. I'd suggest checking with pharmacy first."
